\ The cycle from tail_boundary_mutual_cycle.1z, pinned hybrid. Hybrid compiles `ping` and `pong`
\ as one group after about a hundred calls, so each tail call to the other is a trampoline hop and
\ the cycle runs flat.
\
\ A raise at the bottom of a shorter cycle must carry the interpreted chain: the hops leave no
\ frames behind, as the interpreter's tail calls do not.

pong: ( n -- ) [ 1 - ping ] ;
ping: ( n -- ) [ dup 0 > [ pong ] [ drop "done" print-line ] if ] ;

[ 2000000 ping ] [ error-type: @get . wipe ] recover

bottom-pong: ( n -- ) [ 1 - bottom-ping ] ;
bottom-ping: ( n -- ) [ dup 0 > [ bottom-pong ] [ drop f "bottom" EUserThrown make-error throw ] if ] ;

[ 500 bottom-ping ] [ inspect print-line ] recover
